{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nGit failure strings are classified at five sites with different verdicts for the same text: `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:215,221,517` (index-lock and transient-FS markers, retried locally), `src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py:48,61,110` (non-FF / policy-decline / transport markers), `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock_push.py:68,74` and `_advisory_lock.py:272` (CAS mismatch, terminal), `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:465` (invalid-object recovery). `cannot lock ref` receives three different verdicts; the synthetic `git timed out after` result is produced by three `_git` shims (`push.py:71`, `sync.py:66`, `event_commit_git.py:64`) and treated as retriable by one. Bug `unheedful-custodial-bluebottle` was two of these drifting; `wrongful-chemic-squeaker` added the transient retry to `s3_doctor` only, leaving `sync` and `push_recovery` merges without it.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py`: one marker registry and `classify(result) -> GitOutcome` with kinds `LOCK, TRANSIENT_FS, TRANSPORT, NON_FF, CAS_MISMATCH, POLICY_DECLINE, DIRTY_WD, UNMERGED, FATAL`, the subtractive \"policy wins over non-FF\" rule applied once, and `run_git(..., retry=RetryPolicy)` that folds the timeout shims. Existing predicates become lookups; marker tables move, not change. Guard test: the marker strings (`index.lock`, `non-fast-forward`, `cannot lock ref`, `could not parse head`) appear in `src/rebar` only in `git_outcome.py` (`# git-marker-ok:` escape).\n\n\n## Guard construction\nFollow the guard-test construction rule in the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`: owner module exempt, match the constituent conjunction or AST shape named in Approach (or the definition count where no distinctive atom exists), `# <construct>-ok: <reason>` escape marker, and behaviour pinned only by the named existing tests.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py` (new), `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py`, `src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py`, `src/rebar/_store/push.py`, `src/rebar/_store/sync.py`, `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py`, `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py`, `src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock_push.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py`, `tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nTable-driven test: one captured stderr per kind (taken from the existing tests' fixtures) maps to exactly one kind. Edge: a stderr carrying both `rejected` and a policy-decline marker classifies POLICY_DECLINE. Pinning: `tests/unit/test_gitutil_transient_write_retry.py`, `tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py`, `tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py`, `tests/unit/test_push_rejection_surfacing.py`, `tests/unit/test_push_policy.py`, `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor*.py`, the reconciler ref-lock tests pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every current marker string resolves to one kind and the kind-to-action mapping at each caller is unchanged; checked by the table test plus the pinning suites.\n- [ ] `sync._union_merge` and `push_recovery` merges now retry TRANSIENT_FS faults through the shared `run_git`; checked by a new test injecting `could not parse head` once into a reconverge merge.\n- [ ] The guard test passes and the four `_git` timeout shims are deleted; checked by `grep -rn \"timed out after\" src/rebar/_store`.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787354915581457001,"uuid":"5bbd2efc-e4b7-455e-be46-50dc64cf3b24"}